<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Goldman downgrades Guardian.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Goldman downgrades Guardian.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British insurer Guardian Royal Exchange Plc was cut to &quot;market performer&quot; from &quot;market outperformer&quot; at Goldman Sachs, the investment bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Further detail was not immediately availble. The stock was down 3-1/2p at 280 by 1125 GMT.</p>
<p>On Tuesday the stock fell 4-1/2p after the insurance group said it was considering a major acquisition, countering initial enthusiasm for the shares after results which were in line with analyst expectations.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
